ZN504XG-D voice AFE reset wiring: give the AN7581 AFE node the I2S
reset line so the AFE driver probe can succeed.

Root cause of the voice link failure observed after build-14:

    an7581-audio 1fbe2200.afe: probe with error -2
    sound-slic: snd_soc_register_card fail

The AFE driver introduced by kernel patch 200-02 calls
devm_reset_control_get_exclusive(dev, NULL) during probe.  The mainline
DT binding it was written against (see 201-01) never wired a resets
property into the SoC dtsi, so on a board where the node is enabled the
call returns -ENOENT (-2) and the whole probe fails.  Without the AFE
device there is no PCM host, and the Le9643 sound card registration
fails in turn.

The driver needs only the reset line: it iomaps its single reg resource
and takes no clocks (unlike the dual-resource AFE variant used by older
vendor trees), so one resets property is the entire fix.

The reset provider is the SCU clock/reset controller already present in
an7581.dtsi (scuclk, #reset-cells = <1>), and the binding header with
EN7581_I2S_RST is already included from there, so no new include is
required.  EN7581_I2S_RST == 9 per the mainline binding
include/dt-bindings/reset/airoha,en7581-reset.h.

Depends on 201-04 (adds the &afe status override this patch extends).

Signed-off-by: ZN504XG-D voice porting project
--- a/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi
@@ -410,3 +410,4 @@
 &afe {
 	status = "okay";
+	resets = <&scuclk EN7581_I2S_RST>;
 };
